## My own twist
I added a **PLC Energy Saving** feature. After calculating the costs, the program checks the power rating of each machine and gives a simple status (Low power – OK). This idea was inspired by how PLCs are used in real workshops to monitor and control energy use.

## What I learned
I learned how to collect multiple inputs using lists and loops, how to handle calculations with floats, and the importance of giving clear feedback to the user. I also practised turning a real workshop problem into a simple Python program.

